<Prose title="Privacy" description="What Shot and this website collect, which is nothing.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Shot doesn't collect anything about you. Your screenshots stay on your Mac, in <code>~/Pictures/Shot</code> unless you pick another folder.</p>
  <p>The one time Shot goes online is to check GitHub for updates. It asks before it does that, and you can turn it off in Settings.</p>
  <p>Handing captures to AI agents, which is off unless you turn it on in Settings, only adds a small record inside each capture: which app and window it came from, and what you marked. It stays in the file, so it goes wherever you send the image, and it's why the setting is off by default. The MCP server an agent can connect to reads only your capture folder. It never moves, deletes or changes anything there; the few things it can make, such as a GIF or an annotated copy, are new files beside the capture. It captures or records a window only when you've turned on Let agents capture and record, which is off by default, and only through the running Shot app, which shows a notice each time. An agent's recording always shows the region border and the controls to stop it, never records the microphone or camera, and stops after 10 minutes. Whatever an agent reads, though, goes to that agent's model provider, so blur or pixelate anything private before you hand a capture over.</p>
  <p>This website has no cookies or analytics. Cloudflare hosts it and GitHub hosts the downloads, so <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's</a> privacy policies cover those requests.</p>
  <p>Questions go in <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/shot/issues">GitHub issues</a>.</p>
</Prose>
